    <sectiondef kind="enum">
      <memberdef kind="enum" id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1adf30850e95c6efb72b6d59f5fa167f05" prot="public" static="no" strong="yes">
        <type>uint8</type>
        <name>ETryllHotwordBias</name>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1adf30850e95c6efb72b6d59f5fa167f05a7a1920d61156abc05a60135aefe8bc67" prot="public">
          <name>Default</name>
          <initializer>= 0</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Follow the server catalog: biased when that model&apos;s stt_hotwords_score is non-zero. The zero value, so a manifest written before this field existed keeps its pre-existing behaviour. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1adf30850e95c6efb72b6d59f5fa167f05ad15305d7a4e34e02489c74a5ef542f36" prot="public">
          <name>Off</name>
          <initializer>= 1</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Never bias. Supplying a hotwords lexicon then fails with HotwordBiasDisabled (4106) rather than biasing nothing. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1adf30850e95c6efb72b6d59f5fa167f05a521c36a31c2762741cf0f8890cbe05e3" prot="public">
          <name>On</name>
          <initializer>= 2</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Always bias, lexicon or not. Beam-search decoding is then in force for every session on this model, costing a few percent of decode time and changing its transcripts. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Per-model build selection for this project. Ordinals match the Unity client&apos;s TryllModelRegistration so a shared manifest stays interchangeable. Whether this project wants hotword biasing on an STT model. Mirrors the wire HotwordBias enum.</para>
<para>Unlike ETryllMemoryPlacement this is not a hint the server can quietly downgrade. Biasing requires beam-search decoding, which a recognizer fixes when it is constructed, so the answer decides <emphasis>which</emphasis> recognizer a session is served — and two sessions that disagree about one model hold two of them. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
