      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="enum" id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1a71f0448def7847badc8ca91ef3ac5b76" prot="public" static="no" strong="yes">
        <type>uint8</type>
        <name>ETryllMemoryPlacement</name>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1a71f0448def7847badc8ca91ef3ac5b76a06b9281e396db002010bde1de57262eb" prot="public">
          <name>Auto</name>
          <initializer>= 0</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Server policy decides: device memory when the machine has a usable GPU. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1a71f0448def7847badc8ca91ef3ac5b76ae5d284b6015067eaa11e06b809fe6f13" prot="public">
          <name>Ram</name>
          <initializer>= 1</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>System memory (RAM). </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_tryll_model_manifest_8h_1a71f0448def7847badc8ca91ef3ac5b76a903fb6c788455b69d7c93e06601b03b9" prot="public">
          <name>Vram</name>
          <initializer>= 2</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Device memory (VRAM). </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Where a model&apos;s weights should live. Mirrors the wire MemoryPlacement enum.</para>
<para>Always a hint: a machine that cannot honour it loads the model the other way and reports what it did. That matters here because this value is authored on a developer&apos;s machine and shipped to players&apos; machines — a VRAM choice that suits a 24 GB card is not a promise an 8 GB card can keep.</para>
<para>Which GPU API provides VRAM (CUDA / Vulkan) is deliberately not expressible: that is the host&apos;s decision, not the project&apos;s. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
